{% doc %}
  Resolves whether the Request-for-quote entry points may render for the current customer.
  Returns the string 'true' or 'false' — capture it and compare, the same way callers use
  `can-view-price` / `can-hide-price`:

    {%- capture can_request_quote -%}{%- render 'can-request-quote' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign can_request_quote = can_request_quote | strip -%}
    {%- if can_request_quote == 'true' -%}...{%- endif -%}

  Two gates, both required:
  - the merchant turned `Request for quote` on in Theme settings > B2B features;
  - the visitor is a B2B customer.

  `customer.b2b?` is the only membership test here on purpose. The tag fallback in
  `can-view-price` exists so a merchant can grant *price visibility* to non-B2B customers, but a
  quote request submits a real B2B enquiry — a tag alone should not open it. Collection order
  view is the one place the spec wants quote requests for customers who are NOT yet approved
  (`customer.b2b?` is false for them); that surface needs its own gate and must not reuse this
  snippet.

  Takes no parameters — the answer is customer-wide, not per-product.
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign can_request_quote = false
  if settings.request_for_quote and customer != blank and customer.b2b?
    assign can_request_quote = true
  endif
-%}
{{- can_request_quote -}}
